From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:11:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a thread of an exited child closes no descriptors at
 its exit

pthread_exit_wrapper closes the thread's alert, wait, reply and request
descriptors. On iOS every pseudo-process shares one descriptor table, and
a child's teardown (process_exit_wrapper) closes what the process held. A
thread the server killed with the child and that ends after the teardown
then closed numbers another process had been given since. The childabort
probe's crash phase showed it once killed threads ended at their next
block (madeira-unix 0130): the next child's start failed with c0000008
(its image file closed under it), and a parent worker's server request
failed with EBADF at its exit, after which the parent hung.

Such a thread now closes nothing. What may leak is the thread's own pipes.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-killed-threads.md
Offered-upstream: no; pseudo-processes sharing one descriptor table are the iOS port's
---
 build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
index b333906..4a61e52 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c
@@ -1150,11 +1150,26 @@ static DECLSPEC_NORETURN void pthread_exit_wrapper( int status )
     }
     {
         struct thread_data *data = get_thread_data();
-        close( data->alert_fd );
-        close( data->wait_fd[0] );
-        close( data->wait_fd[1] );
-        close( data->reply_fd );
-        close( data->request_fd );
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+        /* Playport (PLA-222): a thread of a child pseudo-process that has
+         * already exited (one the server killed with it, ending late) closes
+         * nothing. Every pseudo-process shares one descriptor table, the
+         * process's teardown has closed what it held, and the numbers may
+         * belong to another process by now: a crashed child's killed thread
+         * that ended here closed the next child's image file (its start failed
+         * with c0000008) and a parent thread's server pipe (its next request
+         * failed with EBADF and the parent hung). What may leak is the
+         * thread's own pipes. */
+        extern int ios_peb_is_dead_child( void *peb );
+        if (!data->teb || !ios_peb_is_dead_child( data->teb->Peb ))
+#endif
+        {
+            close( data->alert_fd );
+            close( data->wait_fd[0] );
+            close( data->wait_fd[1] );
+            close( data->reply_fd );
+            close( data->request_fd );
+        }
     }
     /* iOS-Madeira (Steam S0): we write the TEB directly into TSD slot 275
      * (start_thread above) because FEX hardcodes offset 0x898 — but we
